    "done_when": "Since routing.picker became route by default (merge 4cb06a148), reckon crew dispatch with --backend codex-terra or --local and no --route refuses with \"picker routing cannot be combined with --backend or --local\" (reckon/cli.py, after resolve_dispatch_route). Measured by a peer at 03:13Z on nova: both forms exited 1 with no worktree, and only --route deterministic --local dispatched. Every session that names its lane now needs a two-step retry.\n\nRequired behaviour:\n1. An explicitly named lane implies deterministic routing when --route was not given. That covers --backend codex-terra (any backend name), --local, and --set default_backend=clive (any backend name). The dispatch goes to the named lane exactly as before the flip, and the run and its ledger row record picker_selection as null, with no picker call.\n2. --route picker given explicitly together with --backend or --local still refuses: the request contradicts itself.\n3. With no lane named and no --route, routing stays as flight resolves it (route under the shipped default).\n4. Check every other entry point that accepts an explicit lane, such as crew redispatch with --backend or a lane change, for the same refusal under the route default, and make each one follow rule 1.\n5. Dry runs report the same route as the real call would.\n\nConfirm the defect reproduces at the base before changing anything: a test dispatching with --backend and no --route, with routing.picker resolving to route, must fail at the base. Tests go in a new tests/test_routing_explicit_lane_implies_deterministic.py, which covers rules 1–3 through the CLI (CliRunner) and asserts that the picker client is never called for an explicit lane. Gate: that file, tests/test_routing_picker_key.py, tests/test_routing_picker_default.py and tests/test_picker_in_dispatch*.py if present. Run them with the main checkout's .venv/bin/python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider, one log for base and one for head under the run directory, judged by delta. The coordinator runs the dispatch population at merge.",
